AuroraSetFitAspect: present the logical framebuffer at a chosen aspect ratio

GameCube behaviour: the console's video output is the 640x480 EFB copy; a game with a 16:9 mode
(or the community 16:9 Gecko code for the game) renders an anamorphic picture into it, and a
widescreen TV stretches that picture horizontally. Dolphin does the same with its "Force 16:9"
aspect setting.

Aurora 3227d76's AURORA_VIEWPORT_FIT sizes the content framebuffer to the window, fitted to the
aspect of the configured render mode (fbWidth x efbHeight, 4:3 for 640x480), and maps logical
viewports, scissors and copies onto it with separate x and y scales. There is no way to present
the logical framebuffer at another aspect while keeping the fit (letterbox/pillarbox) behaviour
on a window of any shape: AURORA_VIEWPORT_STRETCH follows the window exactly.

The patch adds AuroraSetFitAspect(float): 0 (the default) keeps Aurora's behaviour; a positive
value is the aspect FIT keeps instead of the render mode's. Nothing else changes, since
viewports, scissors and texture copies already scale x and y separately. The game's harness sets
it for COS_ASPECT=16:9 or 16:10, where the game draws an anamorphic picture (the widescreen
option, docs/MODS.md).

Upstream status: not reported upstream yet (encounter/aurora at 3227d76).

